sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant U as Player / Court Operator
    participant R as Web app: router
    participant UI as Web app: UI rendering
    participant SA as Web app: scoring actions
    participant AS as Web app: application state
    participant FL as Web app: Firebase listeners / repositories
    participant D as Hub / Beacon / Pulse
    participant I as postEvent
    participant F as Firestore
    participant T as onEventCreate
    participant G as Scoring / Replay
    participant S as score/current
    participant K as Callable functions
    participant O as Overlay / read client
    participant A as Public API

    opt Open a court (/c/{courtId} or /p/{courtId})
        U->>R: Navigate or follow a deep link
        R->>FL: Read the court document
        R->>AS: Enter court session (player or spectator)
        AS->>FL: Attach score + court listeners
        R->>UI: Show the scoreboard view and record history
    end

    alt Browser scoring action
        U->>UI: Score / undo in app
        UI->>SA: addPoint / undoLastPoint
        SA->>UI: Immediate animation + sound feedback
        SA->>FL: Add court event
        FL->>F: Write court event
    else Physical device action
        U->>D: Physical action
        D->>I: POST /postEvent
        I->>F: Append effective event
    end

    opt Beacon changeover active
        I->>I: Apply beaconSidesSwapped for Beacon events
    end

    F-->>T: Event document created
    T->>F: Read court + event + current score
    T->>T: Check scoreVersion and event ordering

    alt Out-of-order event or UNDO
        T->>G: Full active-history replay
    else Normal scoring
        T->>G: Apply event / checkpoint
    end

    G-->>T: Materialized score
    T->>F: Write score/current
    T->>F: Write checkpoint when required
    F-->>S: Updated live score
    S-->>FL: onSnapshot live score
    FL->>AS: Store score in the court session
    AS->>UI: Render points, games, sets, server and badges

    opt Public scoreboard or overlay
        O->>A: GET /revision/{courtId}
        A->>S: Read current score
        A-->>O: Revision payload

        O->>A: GET /score/{courtId}
        A->>S: Read current score
        A-->>O: Live score payload

        O->>A: GET /stats or /momentum
        A->>F: Replay active court history
        A-->>O: Derived payload
    end

    opt Changeover
        UI->>K: changeoverCourt({courtId})
        K->>F: Atomically toggle Beacon mapping + changeoverEvent
        K-->>UI: Success + changeoverEventId
        UI->>AS: Blind-toggle local Changeover state + local Switch Views state
        F-->>FL: Broadcast changeoverEvent to other clients
        FL->>AS: Blind-toggle local Changeover state + local Switch Views state
        AS->>UI: Sync settings tiles, toast and clash cue
    end

    opt RESET
        UI->>K: resetCourt
        K->>F: Archive active events
        K->>F: Delete active events + checkpoints
        K->>F: Reset score/current and Beacon mapping
        K->>F: Increment scoreVersion
    end

    Note over I,D: Current device identity is deviceId/binding. HMAC, freshness, replay protection and idempotency are production targets.
    Note over K,F: Current callable handlers do not perform explicit request.auth checks.
    Note over F,S: Events are authoritative. The current score is derived state.
